'''Jonaes Mendosas i Vidal''' (born 22 September 1986) is a former Balboan security guard who was convicted of the kidnapping and murder of [[Hernandez Lee]], a protester at the [[2021 Carretera Gran Presa del Nord protest]], in [[Tramuntana Province]], [[Balboa]]. Mendosas was employed by [[Nivell de Seguretat]] (NdS) as a security guard at the time of the offence and was deployed to the construction site of the Nou Gran Presa Carretera, where the protest took place on 8 March 2021.

== Early life and employment ==

Jonaes Mendosas i Vidal was born on 22 September 1986 in [[Badia Curta]], [[Jala Province]], a working-class industrial city in the Jala highlands. He grew up in a mixed-race Balboan family in the industrial districts of Badia Curta, where his father worked as a labourer at the chemical plants and his mother was a shop assistant. Mendosas left school at 16 and worked in a series of manual and security jobs before being hired by [[Nivell de Seguretat]] in 2015 as a manned guarding officer.

Mendosas was assigned to the NdS manned guarding division, which provided security for industrial facilities in the Badia Curta zone and, from 2020, for construction sites associated with infrastructure projects in the Tramuntana highlands. He held a valid private security licence issued under Balboan private security regulations and had completed the standard NdS training programme for guarding personnel. His personnel file, reviewed during the subsequent investigation, noted no prior disciplinary issues or complaints.

== 2021 protest and kidnapping ==

{{main|2021 Carretera Gran Presa del Nord protest|Hernandez Lee}}

On 8 March 2021, Mendosas was one of approximately 15 NdS guards deployed to the construction site of the Nou Gran Presa Carretera, where the [[Moviment del poble Birú]] (MPB) had organised a sit-in protest against the road's planned route through Birú sacred caves. During the protest, Mendosas was involved in a physical altercation with [[Hernandez Lee]], a 23-year-old protester and MPB member. The fight was broken up by other protesters and guards.

After the protest concluded in the late afternoon, Mendosas left the construction site in a NdS vehicle. According to the police investigation and court proceedings, Mendosas followed Lee along the [[E8 expressway (Balboa)|E8 expressway]], intercepted him on a remote stretch of the road, and forced him into the vehicle. Mendosas drove Lee to an isolated location in the highlands east of the construction site, where he beat him to death.

Mendosas was arrested on 10 March 2021, two days after the protest, after NdS vehicle records showed that his vehicle had left the construction site after the protest and witness testimony placed him at the altercation with Lee. Lee's body was discovered on 24 March 2021.

== Trial and conviction ==

Mendosas was tried before the Tramuntana Provincial Court in 2022. The prosecution presented vehicle tracking data from the NdS vehicle, witness testimony from protesters and fellow guards, and forensic evidence linking Mendosas to the kidnapping and the site where Lee's body was discovered. The prosecution argued that Mendosas had acted out of personal animosity following the altercation at the protest and had used his position as a security guard and his access to a company vehicle to carry out the kidnapping.

Mendosas pleaded not guilty and testified that he had not followed Lee and had not been involved in his disappearance. The defence argued that the vehicle tracking data was unreliable and that the witness testimony was inconsistent. The court rejected the defence, finding the vehicle tracking data and forensic evidence conclusive.

Mendosas was convicted of kidnapping and murder on 14 June 2022 and sentenced to life imprisonment. He is incarcerated at a federal correctional facility in Tramuntana Province.

== Civil lawsuit ==

{{main|2021 Carretera Gran Presa del Nord protest}}

The family of Hernandez Lee filed a civil lawsuit against Nivell de Seguretat in 2021, seeking damages under the doctrine of {{w|vicarious liability}}, arguing that NdS was responsible for Mendosas's actions as its employee. In 2023, the court found NdS not liable, ruling that Mendosas had acted outside the scope of his employment. The ruling was controversial and was criticised by the [[Moviment del poble Birú]] and the [[Socialist Front of Balboa]] (FSB).

